# Attachment upload = upload relay + single Blob

Do **not** reintroduce HTTP chunking (`/file/chunks/:i`) for new uploads.

## Relays (like relay.encrypt.lu)

| Environment | App host | Upload origin |
|---|---|---|
| Production | `privatenote.ai` | `https://upload.privatenote.ai` |
| Staging (same-site) | `premium.privatenote.ai` | `https://upload-staging.privatenote.ai` |
| Staging (pages.dev) | `premium.privatenote-ai.pages.dev` | `https://upload-staging.privatenote.ai` (cross-site — Safari large bodies fail) |

Resolved by `uploadWorkerOriginForAppHostname()` / `isStagingAppHost()` in `shared/`.

## Same-site requirement (Safari)

encrypt.lu works because SPA and relay share eTLD+1. Test large Safari uploads from:

- Prod: `https://privatenote.ai` → `upload.privatenote.ai`
- Staging: `https://premium.privatenote.ai` → `upload-staging.privatenote.ai`

Not from `*.pages.dev`.

## Flow (Chrome and Safari)

1. Encrypt → one secretstream frame (`totalChunks = 1`)
2. One untyped ciphertext Blob
3. `POST /api/notes/reserve` with exact `plaintext + 17`
4. One `PUT /api/notes/:id/file` to the **upload relay** (not Pages `/api`)
5. Chrome: `fetch` + Bearer · Safari: `xhr.send(blob)` + Bearer
6. Fallbacks: PUT + query token → POST + query token

Never point Safari binary uploads at `*.workers.dev` for large bodies.
